  "content": {
    "id": "p51-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "In how many ways can the integers 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 be placed in a circle if:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p51-q11-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "there are no restrictions,",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5040$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}(8-1)!&=7!\\\\&=5040\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 13
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "all the even numbers are together,",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$576$",
          "worked": "Treat the four even numbers as one unit. With the four odd numbers, there are five units around the circle. The even numbers can be arranged within their unit in $4!$ ways.\n$$\\begin{aligned}N&=(5-1)!\\times4!\\\\&=4!\\times4!\\\\&=576\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "the odd and even numbers alternate,",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$144$",
          "worked": "Fix one odd number and arrange the other three odd numbers in $3!$ ways. Arrange the four even numbers in the four gaps in $4!$ ways.\n$$\\begin{aligned}N&=3!\\times4!\\\\&=144\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q11-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "at least two odd numbers are together,",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4896$",
          "worked": "The complement has no two odd numbers adjacent, so the odd and even numbers alternate, as in part c.\n$$\\begin{aligned}N&=7!-3!\\times4!\\\\&=5040-144\\\\&=4896\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q11-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "the numbers 1 and 7 are adjacent,",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1440$",
          "worked": "Treat 1 and 7 as one unit, giving seven units around the circle. The pair has two internal orders.\n$$\\begin{aligned}N&=(7-1)!\\times2!\\\\&=720\\times2\\\\&=1440\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q11-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "the numbers 3 and 4 are separated?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3600$",
          "worked": "Subtract arrangements with 3 and 4 adjacent from all circular arrangements.\n$$\\begin{aligned}N&=7!-2\\times6!\\\\&=5040-1440\\\\&=3600\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      }
    ]
  },
